WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.750
The drive from my home
to Holy Cross Church

00:00:04.750 --> 00:00:07.583
is only a couple of miles away

00:00:07.583 --> 00:00:10.625
and every single day
I pass by that church,

00:00:10.625 --> 00:00:12.375
you're always remembering
what happened to you.

00:00:12.375 --> 00:00:13.416
Where you were.

00:00:14.416 --> 00:00:16.333
The pain and the anguish that you suffered

00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:18.375
as a young little kid is
never gonna be diminished.

00:00:18.375 --> 00:00:19.750
It's never gonna go away.

00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:23.625
Also knowing that where
I learned about God

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.833
was also where I learned about pain.

00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:33.541
There are thousands of me
all across the country

00:00:33.541 --> 00:00:34.458
and still to this day

00:00:34.458 --> 00:00:36.958
there are some of us that
have never come forward

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:38.416
and will never come forward

00:00:38.416 --> 00:00:40.458
because they're afraid
of what their community,

00:00:40.458 --> 00:00:43.125
what their family and their
friends are going to say.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.625
I was very nervous about speaking out

00:00:47.625 --> 00:00:49.541
against the Catholic Church

00:00:49.541 --> 00:00:51.958
but this is not about the church.

00:00:51.958 --> 00:00:55.250
This is about what's doing
right for the victims.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:56.041
Good evening.

00:00:56.041 --> 00:00:58.583
Two men are taking on two
Albuquerque Catholic Churches

00:00:58.583 --> 00:01:00.083
and the archdiocese.

00:01:00.083 --> 00:01:02.166
They say they were raped as boys

00:01:02.166 --> 00:01:04.458
and accused the church of covering it up.

00:01:04.458 --> 00:01:08.416
The diocese is aware of about
500 claims against them.

00:01:08.416 --> 00:01:09.708
The Archdiocese of Milwaukee

00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:12.541
said it must file for
bankruptcy for reorganization.

00:01:12.541 --> 00:01:14.500
The diocese says it filed for bankruptcy

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:17.541
because of clergy sex abuse payouts.

00:01:17.541 --> 00:01:19.250
The numbers were shocking.

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:21.583
The number of pedophile priests,

00:01:21.583 --> 00:01:25.041
the amount of assets that
were being transferred

00:01:25.041 --> 00:01:27.833
back to the parishes across the country,

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:31.916
or back to the Vatican, so
that the Catholic Church

00:01:31.916 --> 00:01:33.958
doesn't have to pay their victims.

00:01:33.958 --> 00:01:36.666
A lot of archdiocese,
before they file bankruptcy

00:01:36.666 --> 00:01:38.500
they make moves, shift assets,

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:42.000
they recategorize assets
in ways that shrink

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.291
the pot of money that's
available to victims.

00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:46.291
This is a story about money and a church

00:01:46.291 --> 00:01:47.916
acting more like a corporation

00:01:47.916 --> 00:01:49.500
than a faith-based institution.

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:56.583
My name is Josh Saul.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:59.333
I'm a reporter for Bloomberg
News and Businessweek

00:01:59.333 --> 00:02:02.166
and I wrote a story
about the Catholic Church

00:02:02.166 --> 00:02:04.750
and how it uses bankruptcy
to shield its money

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.583
from sex abuse victims.

00:02:07.500 --> 00:02:08.791
For most of the 1900s,

00:02:08.791 --> 00:02:11.583
the way the Catholic Church
dealt with claims of sex abuse,

00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:12.791
which at that point was usually

00:02:12.791 --> 00:02:15.708
just a mother coming forward and saying,

00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:17.833
my child tells me that this happened,

00:02:17.833 --> 00:02:19.250
was they would cover it up.

00:02:19.250 --> 00:02:21.750
Church leaders would say,
we're sorry about this.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.083
We'll handle it.

00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:25.250
That priest will be
disciplined or transferred

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:26.125
and it mostly worked.

00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:27.541
They mostly kept it under wraps.

00:02:27.541 --> 00:02:30.333
So there was an awakening in the '90s

00:02:30.333 --> 00:02:32.708
that there was a problem

00:02:32.708 --> 00:02:35.666
that began to appear to be systemic.

00:02:36.916 --> 00:02:38.541
And then we come to find out,

00:02:38.541 --> 00:02:41.250
historically it's always been happening.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.208
It's just, it's been kept quiet.

00:02:44.708 --> 00:02:45.541
I'm Merit Bennett.

00:02:45.541 --> 00:02:48.250
I'm a lawyer in Santa Fe, New Mexico.

00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.791
We have have represented
between 100 and 150 cases.

00:02:51.791 --> 00:02:52.833
Could be more,

00:02:52.833 --> 00:02:55.791
that's my best recollection.

00:02:56.875 --> 00:03:01.125
They came to us in shame
and that was the tactic.

00:03:01.125 --> 00:03:04.250
We will make everybody feel ashamed

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:09.208
if they reveal the secret
that we're trying to tamp down

00:03:09.208 --> 00:03:11.958
and put in the cupboard and it worked.

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:16.458
But there was still this
breakthrough into the public arena.

00:03:16.458 --> 00:03:18.916
In the '80s and '90s, people
started to file lawsuits

00:03:18.916 --> 00:03:20.833
against the church when they themselves

00:03:20.833 --> 00:03:23.625
or when their children were
sexually abused by priests.

00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:29.583
The Catholic Church quickly
moved to set up a system

00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:32.875
to quote, "mediate these cases."

00:03:32.875 --> 00:03:35.166
In other words, to try to get them settled.

00:03:35.166 --> 00:03:37.166
Between the early 1980s and 2002,

00:03:37.166 --> 00:03:41.708
church leaders paid about $750
million in quiet settlements.

00:03:41.708 --> 00:03:43.250
What changed was in 2002,

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.291
the Boston Globe, its Spotlight team,

00:03:45.291 --> 00:03:48.625
exposed for the first time
how priests in that city,

00:03:48.625 --> 00:03:50.333
and how church
leadership in that city

00:03:50.333 --> 00:03:52.583
had abused a huge number of children

00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:56.083
and had conspired to keep it all a secret.

00:03:56.125 --> 00:03:58.875
And so that created a whole second wave,

00:03:58.875 --> 00:04:00.500
really, throughout the country

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.958
and there's been a movie
made about it since.

00:04:04.416 --> 00:04:08.750
They knew, and they let it happen to kids.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:09.708
Okay?

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:10.916
It could have been you.

00:04:10.916 --> 00:04:11.875
It could have been me.

00:04:11.875 --> 00:04:13.208
It could have been any of us.

00:04:13.416 --> 00:04:16.291
When larger numbers of people
started to file lawsuits

00:04:16.291 --> 00:04:18.000
about the fact that they were abused,

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:21.333
churches couldn't handle
those on a case-by-case basis.

00:04:21.333 --> 00:04:24.500
So then church leaders
had to file bankruptcy

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:27.125
in order to deal with a
large number of lawsuits.

00:04:27.125 --> 00:04:31.416
I was used to covering bankruptcies
of Toys "R" Us or Sears,

00:04:31.416 --> 00:04:33.791
big companies that filed for bankruptcy

00:04:33.791 --> 00:04:35.666
but this was a totally
different situation,

00:04:35.666 --> 00:04:37.208
this was a church.

00:04:37.625 --> 00:04:38.833
We begin with the top story

00:04:38.833 --> 00:04:40.750
that we've been following all day.

00:04:40.750 --> 00:04:44.291
After years of turmoil, the
Catholic Diocese of Buffalo

00:04:44.291 --> 00:04:46.125
has filed for bankruptcy.

00:04:46.125 --> 00:04:47.541
The Archdiocese of Milwaukee

00:04:47.541 --> 00:04:49.291
said it must file for bankruptcy.

00:04:49.291 --> 00:04:51.791
The Diocese of Rockville
Centre is filing for bankruptcy.

00:04:51.791 --> 00:04:54.916
Almost 30 dioceses or
church districts in the U.S.

00:04:54.916 --> 00:04:56.958
have filed bankruptcy since 2004.

00:04:56.958 --> 00:04:59.291
There were at least six bankruptcies

00:04:59.291 --> 00:05:01.250
by Catholic Churches in 2020.

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:02.416
That's a huge increase.

00:05:02.416 --> 00:05:03.708
There have been years in the past

00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:05.750
where there wasn't a single bankruptcy.

00:05:05.750 --> 00:05:07.458
There were periods where
it would take several years

00:05:07.458 --> 00:05:09.083
to get to six bankruptcies.

00:05:09.083 --> 00:05:10.500
There's been a huge increase

00:05:10.500 --> 00:05:12.791
in the number of bankruptcies
by church districts.

00:05:13.375 --> 00:05:16.291
If you're an abuse victim
and you have a lawsuit

00:05:16.291 --> 00:05:17.708
that you filed against the church,

00:05:17.708 --> 00:05:20.583
when the church files for
bankruptcy your lawsuit is frozen.

00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:22.500
It's brought into the bankruptcy

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:24.208
and then your only option at that point

00:05:24.208 --> 00:05:26.000
is to hope for a good settlement.

00:05:26.333 --> 00:05:28.250
Church leaders benefit in a number of ways

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:29.583
when they file for bankruptcy.

00:05:29.583 --> 00:05:32.625
First, it creates one
central streamlined process

00:05:32.625 --> 00:05:35.791
to deal with all of the
sexual abuse lawsuits.

00:05:35.791 --> 00:05:37.333
Two, you get a bar.

00:05:37.333 --> 00:05:38.458
After the bankruptcy,

00:05:38.458 --> 00:05:41.500
nobody can file a lawsuit
over a past abuse.

00:05:41.500 --> 00:05:42.666
It's basically a clean slate,

00:05:42.666 --> 00:05:44.791
as one lawyer described it to me.

00:05:44.791 --> 00:05:47.625
And three, bankruptcy is a quieter process

00:05:47.625 --> 00:05:50.000
than a big civil lawsuit.

00:05:50.250 --> 00:05:53.833
The bankrupt, the
archdiocese has to account

00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:57.000
and disclose all of its assets.

00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:59.666
All of its money, all of its property,

00:05:59.666 --> 00:06:03.083
all of its real estate as
part of the bankrupt estate

00:06:03.083 --> 00:06:04.500
so we know what we're dealing with,

00:06:04.500 --> 00:06:06.625
all of its debts and so forth and so on.

00:06:06.625 --> 00:06:10.541
When we first brought these
cases back in the '90s,

00:06:11.458 --> 00:06:13.416
we were hearing rumors

00:06:13.416 --> 00:06:18.375
that real estate was being
put into blind trusts.

00:06:18.791 --> 00:06:22.333
A lot of transfers of
assets were going on.

00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:28.000
They could see, foresee the
avalanche down the road.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.416
So what my reporting showed
is that a lot of archdiocese,

00:06:30.416 --> 00:06:33.375
before they file
bankruptcy, they make moves.

00:06:33.375 --> 00:06:36.416
They shift assets, they
recategorize assets

00:06:36.416 --> 00:06:39.166
in ways that shrink the pot of money

00:06:39.166 --> 00:06:40.875
that's available to victims.

00:06:40.875 --> 00:06:44.500
So I did a lot of work
to try to put a number

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.250
on the amount of money
that the church had moved

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:50.500
from assets that it owned to its parishes

00:06:50.500 --> 00:06:53.625
or to various foundations
or cemetery foundations.

00:06:53.625 --> 00:06:57.041
And after adding up everything
from big, big bankruptcies,

00:06:57.041 --> 00:07:00.208
like Minneapolis to smaller
ones like Gallup, New Mexico

00:07:00.208 --> 00:07:01.750
and all the way back to San Diego,

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:03.833
the number that I came
up with was $2 billion.

00:07:04.541 --> 00:07:08.666
If you imagine an organization
that files for bankruptcy

00:07:08.666 --> 00:07:13.666
and they have $100 million in
assets, that's a lot of money.

00:07:13.666 --> 00:07:15.916
That's a lot of assets
that can then be divided up

00:07:15.916 --> 00:07:17.666
among victims in a settlement.

00:07:17.666 --> 00:07:20.208
If you have that same
organization, but they say,

00:07:20.208 --> 00:07:23.291
oh, we actually only have $5 million in assets.

00:07:23.291 --> 00:07:25.166
That's a much smaller pot of money

00:07:25.166 --> 00:07:26.875
that can be divided up among victims.

00:07:28.541 --> 00:07:31.583
To boil it down, the church shifted money.

00:07:31.583 --> 00:07:34.625
Critics would say that
they hid money into places

00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:37.666
where it was not available
for clergy abuse victims.

00:07:41.958 --> 00:07:44.458
Santa Fe is a very beautiful community

00:07:44.458 --> 00:07:48.708
that is steeped in tradition and culture.

00:07:48.708 --> 00:07:51.583
It is a predominantly Catholic community

00:07:51.583 --> 00:07:56.166
where individuals focus
and tend to have deep pride

00:07:56.166 --> 00:07:57.833
in their traditions and the cultures

00:07:57.833 --> 00:08:00.083
that they've been
practicing for centuries.

00:08:00.583 --> 00:08:04.333
As a young kid, I was raised
Catholic, went to confirmation,

00:08:04.333 --> 00:08:07.666
went through all of my catechism
classes as a young kid.

00:08:07.666 --> 00:08:10.291
I went to Catholic school my entire life.

00:08:10.291 --> 00:08:12.958
And so religion was a part of me.

00:08:12.958 --> 00:08:17.958
The church that I was a part
of is Santa Cruz de La Cañada.

00:08:18.666 --> 00:08:21.333
So as a young kid, I thought
I was going to become a priest.

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:23.625
Being a part of the
Catholic Church community,

00:08:23.625 --> 00:08:26.125
I think as a young kid, you have reverence

00:08:26.125 --> 00:08:28.875
and you see these priests
and you want to emulate them.

00:08:31.083 --> 00:08:33.958
My life changed drastically

00:08:33.958 --> 00:08:37.541
right around the age of 10 years of age.

00:08:37.541 --> 00:08:40.958
I kind of hold myself to the position

00:08:40.958 --> 00:08:43.333
that I allowed my guard to be down.

00:08:43.333 --> 00:08:44.666
That's when he took advantage

00:08:44.666 --> 00:08:49.583
and I think as a young kid, it
really screws with your mind

00:08:49.583 --> 00:08:52.958
because you wonder what you did wrong,

00:08:52.958 --> 00:08:55.791
and you wonder why it was you?

00:08:57.083 --> 00:08:59.208
I'm now 38 years of age.

00:08:59.208 --> 00:09:02.166
You deal with this issue every single day

00:09:02.166 --> 00:09:05.583
and so for me, my biggest challenge was

00:09:05.583 --> 00:09:08.416
I knew I was harmed and
I was hurt as a young kid

00:09:08.416 --> 00:09:10.375
by this individual, all of us do.

00:09:10.375 --> 00:09:12.750
But the real harm and the real hurt

00:09:12.750 --> 00:09:15.583
comes from the fact of what the Vatican,

00:09:15.583 --> 00:09:17.791
what the Archdiocese of Santa Fe,

00:09:17.791 --> 00:09:20.791
what all these other
organizations have done

00:09:20.791 --> 00:09:24.000
to hide this issue and to brush it away

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.583
like it was no big issue.

00:09:25.583 --> 00:09:27.625
That's really where the
big hurt comes from.

00:09:27.625 --> 00:09:30.916
These are the organizations
that should be protecting us.

00:09:32.583 --> 00:09:35.208
By the archdiocese filing for bankruptcy,

00:09:35.208 --> 00:09:36.791
they have essentially told every victim

00:09:36.791 --> 00:09:37.750
that they don't care.

00:09:37.750 --> 00:09:38.708
Breaking news right now.

00:09:38.708 --> 00:09:41.375
The Archdiocese of Santa
Fe filing for bankruptcy,

00:09:41.375 --> 00:09:42.208
we have learned.

00:09:42.208 --> 00:09:43.916
The archbishop just called a meeting

00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:47.166
with every priest in the
diocese to a mandatory meeting

00:09:47.166 --> 00:09:48.250
where he made that announcement.

00:09:48.250 --> 00:09:49.916
Now, the diocese attorney says

00:09:49.916 --> 00:09:53.125
they are currently handling 35 to 40 cases

00:09:53.125 --> 00:09:54.833
from people claiming sexual abuse

00:09:54.833 --> 00:09:57.166
at the hands of different
Catholic priests.

00:09:57.166 --> 00:09:59.250
They have already paid millions of dollars

00:09:59.250 --> 00:10:02.375
to victims and survivors,
but by filing bankruptcy,

00:10:02.375 --> 00:10:05.750
future victims will be waiting
longer for compensation.

00:10:06.541 --> 00:10:09.250
There ended up being over
300 sexual abuse lawsuits

00:10:09.250 --> 00:10:12.916
filed against the Archdiocese
of Santa Fe in its bankruptcy.

00:10:12.916 --> 00:10:14.333
Which is kind of amazing to think about,

00:10:14.333 --> 00:10:15.791
New Mexico is not a big state.

00:10:15.791 --> 00:10:18.583
Finally, the archdiocese cracked

00:10:18.583 --> 00:10:21.416
and by cracked, I mean
they filed bankruptcy.

00:10:21.416 --> 00:10:26.333
They basically did that
not because, in my opinion,

00:10:26.333 --> 00:10:30.333
that they couldn't afford
to pay these claims.

00:10:30.333 --> 00:10:32.583
They made it as a business decision,

00:10:32.583 --> 00:10:37.458
they thought that this would
basically save them money.

00:10:37.458 --> 00:10:39.791
So when the Archdiocese in
Santa Fe filed for bankruptcy

00:10:39.791 --> 00:10:44.708
in late 2018, it said we
have $49 million in assets.

00:10:44.708 --> 00:10:48.375
But on the same filing,
it also listed $91 million

00:10:48.375 --> 00:10:50.750
that it either held on
behalf of its parishes

00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:52.958
or that it had transferred
to its parishes.

00:10:52.958 --> 00:10:54.250
So when Isaac and I drove around

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.291
and saw sign after sign after sign

00:10:56.291 --> 00:10:58.333
saying welcome to the
Archdiocese of Santa Fe

00:10:58.416 --> 00:11:00.375
on all of these different parishes,

00:11:00.375 --> 00:11:03.875
it again seemed to show to
me the close relationship

00:11:03.875 --> 00:11:06.083
between the archdiocese and its parishes.

00:11:27.125 --> 00:11:30.083
So the Archdiocese of Santa
Fe, it's a big organization

00:11:30.083 --> 00:11:32.625
it has a CFO, it has a
Chief Financial Officer.

00:11:32.625 --> 00:11:34.500
For a long, long time
it's been the same guy.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:35.750
His name is Tony Salgado.

00:11:35.750 --> 00:11:37.750
You know, people I talked to
said like, Tony is a great guy,

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:38.708
he's a really nice guy.

00:11:38.708 --> 00:11:41.166
He wouldn't talk to me, which makes sense.

00:11:41.166 --> 00:11:44.083
One lawyer described to me, he
knows where all the money is.

00:11:44.083 --> 00:11:47.416
He is the one who put
into effect transfers

00:11:47.416 --> 00:11:50.958
and the categorizations that
shrank the amount of money

00:11:50.958 --> 00:11:52.541
that is available to victims.

00:11:53.291 --> 00:11:55.666
So in 2012, Tony Salgado called a meeting.

00:11:55.666 --> 00:11:57.666
They gathered the business managers

00:11:57.666 --> 00:11:59.708
for its 90 parishes from across the state.

00:11:59.708 --> 00:12:02.083
They gathered them all
together in a conference room

00:12:02.083 --> 00:12:04.333
in Albuquerque at
archdiocese headquarters.

00:12:04.333 --> 00:12:06.583
And they told them that
each business manager

00:12:06.583 --> 00:12:09.208
needed to incorporate
their parish separately.

00:12:09.916 --> 00:12:11.583
My name's Christine Romero

00:12:11.583 --> 00:12:18.125
and I worked for the Archdiocese
of Santa Fe for 12 years.

00:12:19.333 --> 00:12:23.208
The meeting was sometime
the summer of 2012.

00:12:23.208 --> 00:12:25.916
The business managers were called together

00:12:25.916 --> 00:12:32.708
to help us understand how
to incorporate the parishes.

00:12:34.666 --> 00:12:36.208
What that has the effect of doing

00:12:36.208 --> 00:12:37.708
is it means that all of those assets

00:12:37.708 --> 00:12:38.791
that are owned by the church,

00:12:38.791 --> 00:12:41.541
its building, its collection
plate, its parking lot,

00:12:41.541 --> 00:12:45.208
all of that is owned by the
parish, not by the archdiocese.

00:12:47.708 --> 00:12:50.958
I didn't really have any

00:12:50.958 --> 00:12:55.625
either negative or positive
ideas about the incorporation.

00:12:55.625 --> 00:12:59.333
But when I did ask what the impact

00:12:59.333 --> 00:13:03.541
was gonna be on the parishes
on my particular workload,

00:13:03.541 --> 00:13:05.125
I asked Tony Salgado.

00:13:05.125 --> 00:13:08.416
He said that there would be no difference,

00:13:08.416 --> 00:13:11.250
that our work would be exactly the same,

00:13:11.250 --> 00:13:17.458
that we were incorporating
each parish separately

00:13:17.458 --> 00:13:21.541
to protect the parishes
from the pedophile lawsuits

00:13:21.541 --> 00:13:24.833
that were coming in to the archdiocese.

00:13:24.833 --> 00:13:28.333
So when Christine told me
that, it was a pretty big deal.

00:13:28.333 --> 00:13:29.958
I'm like, okay, great smoking gun.

00:13:31.333 --> 00:13:33.125
I decided to go on the record

00:13:33.125 --> 00:13:36.958
because I don't believe
the Catholic Church

00:13:36.958 --> 00:13:39.291
should care about money.

00:13:39.291 --> 00:13:43.375
We're about protecting
our faith, not our money.

00:13:43.375 --> 00:13:49.333
If we have had abusive
priests, pedophile priests,

00:13:49.375 --> 00:13:53.791
that's so unfortunate, but
if we have to sell our land

00:13:53.791 --> 00:13:58.625
or sell our assets to help the victims,

00:13:58.625 --> 00:14:00.083
I think we should do that.

00:14:00.083 --> 00:14:02.583
I don't believe that we should be

00:14:02.583 --> 00:14:05.875
protecting monetary
items, material things.

00:14:05.875 --> 00:14:08.083
That's not what our faith is based on.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:13.458
I just didn't realize the bigger picture

00:14:13.458 --> 00:14:17.000
of what was happening on a larger scale

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.583
in terms of lawsuits.

00:14:19.583 --> 00:14:20.958
I knew at a national level

00:14:20.958 --> 00:14:23.666
there was a lot of pedophile lawsuits.

00:14:23.666 --> 00:14:26.833
I just didn't realize the magnitude

00:14:26.833 --> 00:14:29.250
and the number of lawsuits

00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:31.166
that were happening in New Mexico.

00:14:32.583 --> 00:14:35.083
Tony Salgado has not
responded to these claims.

00:14:35.083 --> 00:14:36.541
He's emailed me back only to say

00:14:36.541 --> 00:14:38.541
that I would need to talk to the lawyer

00:14:38.541 --> 00:14:39.750
representing the church.

00:14:48.958 --> 00:14:50.875
By incorporating the parishes separately

00:14:50.875 --> 00:14:54.250
and also by moving parish
assets into a trust,

00:14:54.250 --> 00:14:58.666
the archdiocese moved about
$91 million off of its books

00:14:58.666 --> 00:15:00.708
into accounts or trusts.

00:15:02.625 --> 00:15:04.625
By studying past bankruptcy settlements,

00:15:04.625 --> 00:15:06.208
I came up with a very rough estimate

00:15:06.208 --> 00:15:10.708
which was archdiocese often
settle for half of the assets

00:15:10.708 --> 00:15:12.833
that they initially say that they owned

00:15:12.833 --> 00:15:14.291
when they filed for bankruptcy.

00:15:14.291 --> 00:15:16.583
So using the 50% number as a rough guide,

00:15:16.583 --> 00:15:18.750
victims in Santa Fe could expect to get

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:21.166
about $65,000 in the settlement

00:15:21.166 --> 00:15:23.041
if the church stuck to saying

00:15:23.041 --> 00:15:25.750
that it owned just $49 million in assets.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:28.625
But if the archdiocese included
all of this other money

00:15:28.625 --> 00:15:30.375
from its parishes, its foundation,

00:15:30.375 --> 00:15:32.166
then victims could
expect to get a lot more,

00:15:32.166 --> 00:15:33.666
more like $300,000.

00:15:35.416 --> 00:15:37.583
I did a lot of reporting
to try and understand

00:15:37.583 --> 00:15:39.250
what happens after someone's abused.

00:15:39.250 --> 00:15:41.583
I talked to a psychiatrist in Santa Fe

00:15:41.583 --> 00:15:43.041
who treats a lot of these victims.

00:15:43.041 --> 00:15:44.041
Basically what I learned

00:15:44.041 --> 00:15:45.583
is that being a victim is expensive.

00:15:45.583 --> 00:15:48.250
Researchers at Johns Hopkins
actually put a number on it.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:51.000
Childhood sexual abuse can end up costing

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:53.916
that victim $280,000
throughout their lifetime.

00:15:55.166 --> 00:15:57.208
For me personally, as a victim,

00:15:57.208 --> 00:15:59.958
I don't always believe that
money fixes everything.

00:15:59.958 --> 00:16:03.000
A sense of community and
a sense of counselling

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:06.458
and rehabilitation is more important.

00:16:06.458 --> 00:16:10.250
Money is just the Band-Aid
that fixes a scrape,

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:13.500
but we're not really looking
as to what caused the scrape.

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:16.541
We're not looking at the
long-term effects of that.

00:16:16.541 --> 00:16:20.791
And so there needs to be
a strong sense of movement

00:16:20.791 --> 00:16:24.291
to getting people the
help that is continuous

00:16:24.291 --> 00:16:26.458
and isn't just temporary.

00:16:37.958 --> 00:16:41.125
How do you value the damage

00:16:41.125 --> 00:16:43.333
that this inflicts on a human being?

00:16:43.333 --> 00:16:45.000
Money's not gonna fix it totally,

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:49.583
but certainly it could begin
to help get people access

00:16:49.583 --> 00:16:53.916
to mental health care, to get
them to rebuild their lives

00:16:53.916 --> 00:16:55.625
and be able to find a job

00:16:55.625 --> 00:16:59.625
and try to come back to believing
that it's not their fault.

00:17:00.375 --> 00:17:02.541
But things are changing
in a couple of ways.

00:17:02.541 --> 00:17:04.875
The bankruptcies now are very contentious.

00:17:04.875 --> 00:17:07.333
The victims in Santa Fe actually just won

00:17:07.333 --> 00:17:09.708
a court decision where
they can now sue the church

00:17:09.708 --> 00:17:13.041
to bring some of those assets
back into the pot of money

00:17:13.041 --> 00:17:14.458
that the archdiocese owns.

00:17:15.708 --> 00:17:18.583
So here we are with the
archdiocese of Santa Fe

00:17:18.583 --> 00:17:22.458
now facing scrutiny that
they've never faced before.

00:17:22.458 --> 00:17:26.041
So I'm not sure where the
Catholic Church goes with this.

00:17:26.833 --> 00:17:29.583
This is not unusual, by the way.

00:17:29.583 --> 00:17:32.291
This has happened around the world.

00:17:32.291 --> 00:17:34.416
Certainly when these types of claims

00:17:34.416 --> 00:17:38.958
that threatened these
assets started to arrive,

00:17:38.958 --> 00:17:40.333
everything went underground

00:17:40.333 --> 00:17:42.541
as far as their holdings are concerned.

00:17:43.291 --> 00:17:45.875
So that's kind of where we are now.

00:18:05.875 --> 00:18:07.875
My hope for this story is
that it shows the people

00:18:07.875 --> 00:18:10.125
around these bankruptcies,
from the victims,

00:18:10.125 --> 00:18:11.958
to the lawyers, to the church leaders

00:18:11.958 --> 00:18:13.333
what's happened in the past,

00:18:13.333 --> 00:18:16.083
helps them understand
what's going to be happening

00:18:16.083 --> 00:18:16.916
at an even greater rate

00:18:16.916 --> 00:18:19.041
as more and more churches
file for bankruptcy

00:18:19.041 --> 00:18:20.083
in the years to come.

00:18:22.333 --> 00:18:24.875
I think this issue of child molestation

00:18:24.875 --> 00:18:28.000
and bankruptcy is predominant
all across the country,

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.250
from Los Angeles, to
Chicago, to Milwaukee.

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:35.500
These are issues that have
occurred from the highest order

00:18:35.500 --> 00:18:37.958
all the way down to seminarians.

00:18:37.958 --> 00:18:39.666
And young kids have been caught

00:18:39.666 --> 00:18:43.083
in this whirlwind for decades.

00:18:43.083 --> 00:18:49.916
I just want to reassure the
victims of pedophile priests

00:18:49.916 --> 00:18:54.125
that there are some
Catholics who do understand

00:18:54.125 --> 00:18:58.166
and who do sympathize
and who do support them

00:18:58.166 --> 00:19:02.416
in their lawsuits and in getting

00:19:02.416 --> 00:19:05.458
whatever monetary compensation they need,

00:19:05.458 --> 00:19:08.250
to make them and their
families whole again.

00:19:09.458 --> 00:19:11.333
I think we're about to hit the key point

00:19:11.333 --> 00:19:15.000
and we'll see what the church,
how they respond to this.

